  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...High pressure will bring above normal temps and \nmainly dry weather through early Saturday with above normal rain \nchances later Saturday into early Monday as a front wavers in \nthe area.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nHigh pressure will continue into early Sat keeping a warming trend \nthrough Fri night. Highs around 90 are likely inland today with \nhumidity slowly continuing to increase. Rain chances will be on the \nincrease later Saturday as high pressure weakens, a cold front \napproaches and moisture/upper forcing increase. Rain chances should \nremain above normal through early Mon as the front slows down and \nlingers over or near the area. Trends favor a drier Monday, \nespecially for northern/western areas, so confidence in the latest \nforecast rain chances is low. At least there is a decent chance for \nbeneficial rainfall over an inch, which would be very welcome \nconsidering the ongoing drought in most areas. Not expecting any \nrisk for severe storms, although locally heavy rainfall could \nproduce minor flooding.",
